  "scope": "Retained ordinary single-column indexed LONG UPDATE, TCNI26 original and V3 recovery, actual CREATE/save/reopen/UPDATE workflows; separate 16,385-row unindexed batch scale check.",
  "qualification": "Independent complete-image, recovery and headless application evidence. No Microsoft Access/Windows comparison or statistical performance benchmark.",
  "observations": [
    "Indexed-target metadata selects TCNI26 for zero, one or multiple original assignments; unindexed TCNI24/17/25 routes retain separate selection. Complete source and constraints remain consuming checks.",
    "Native checks cover actual index creation, nullable and duplicate key ties, multiple levels and directions, a 200,000-row source, all 16,385 selected rows, 20-hop forwarding and Currency/Unicode preservation.",
    "All original assignments bind before the merged DATA/INDEX candidate. Independent proof reconstructs source records and complete final index membership and compares the entire image. Existing unique/Required constraints accept valid edits and refuse violations.",
    "The separate original and V3 recovery retain original requests and BEFORE identity; old original families and no-create builds remain closed. Failed decoding is not retried as another action.",
    "Full adapter/runtime suites and selected normal Desktop SQL Run tests cover CREATE/save/acknowledgment/reopen followed by indexed UPDATE No/Yes/save/acknowledgment/reopen and fresh ordered reads. Late assignment failures preserve source and existing results.",
    "ROW-key preparation uses a paid sorted borrowed request directory, retaining all matching original updates and their input order. Independent proof builds its own directory; producer patches and membership are not its oracle.",
    "A separate unindexed operation updates all 16,385 selected original rows and compares the complete independently authored AFTER. Its explicit caller work allowance is not a resident-memory measurement or Access file limit.",
    "Commands use release mode and workspace-root target/. Test counts overlap and are not a conformance percentage; 117 selected native and one runtime fixture-dependent tests are ignored, not passing evidence."
  ],
